1. LiveBench question pool — internal/router/benchdata/pool.json
================================================================================

WHAT IT IS

  internal/router/benchdata/pool.json is a 656,634-byte snapshot of 356
  questions and their ground-truth answers taken from LiveBench (ICLR 2025,
  https://livebench.ai, https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.19314,
  https://huggingface.co/livebench).

  The file records its own provenance in two top-level fields:

      fetched_at   2026-08-08T04:28:04Z
      source       https://huggingface.co/livebench — LiveBench, ICLR 2025
                   (arxiv.org/abs/2406.19314)

  The third top-level field, `questions`, holds the 356 records. Each carries
  eight fields: id, category, task, match, prompt, expect, release_date,
  retired. There is no per-question licence field and no per-question source
  URL, so the terms below apply to the file as a whole and, where noted, to
  named subsets of it.

  The snapshot is used by the `bench` developer subcommands to calibrate and
  select benchmark questions. It is committed rather than fetched at build time
  because the question set is part of the worker profile cache key: if the
  questions could change without the version changing, workers profiled on
  different days would be graded on different sets and then compared on the same
  0-100 scale.


LICENCE, AND WHERE THAT GRANT IS ACTUALLY STATED

  LiveBench's stated licence is the Apache License, Version 2.0. A full copy of
  that licence is included at LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt, as required by section
  4(a).

  The grant is worth citing precisely, because it is not where you would first
  look for it. It appears in two places:

    - The LiveBench paper, Appendix B.1 ("Author Responsibility and License").
    - docs/DATASHEET.md in the LiveBench repository: "The benchmark suite is
      public as of June 12, 2024, distributed under the Apache License 2.0."

  It does NOT appear in the LiveBench repository's own LICENSE file. That file
  contains copied FastChat and LiveCodeBench licences and is not a grant from
  the LiveBench authors covering the benchmark data. GitHub's licence detector
  reports NOASSERTION for the repository as a result, and the HuggingFace
  dataset cards for livebench/math and livebench/reasoning carry no licence
  field at all. Anyone auditing this repository who checks only those three
  surfaces will conclude the data is unlicensed. It is licensed; the grant is in
  the paper and the datasheet.


MODIFICATIONS (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))

  This project modified the LiveBench material before redistributing it. The
  changes are:

    - SUBSET. Only the `math` and `reasoning` datasets were taken, and within
      them only four tasks: math_comp, olympiad, zebra_puzzle and spatial.
      LiveBench's other categories (coding, agentic coding, data analysis,
      instruction following, language) are not present, nor is the AMPS_Hard
      task. Rows whose prompt exceeds 6000 characters, rows with no ground
      truth, and multi-turn rows were dropped.

    - RESHAPE. Each row was flattened from LiveBench's dataset schema into the
      eight-field JSON record described above: `question_id` becomes `id`, the
      dataset name becomes `category`, `turns[0]` becomes `prompt`,
      `ground_truth` becomes `expect`, `livebench_release_date` becomes
      `release_date`, and the presence of `livebench_removal_date` becomes the
      boolean `retired`. Upstream columns not listed here were dropped. A
      `match` field naming this project's grader was added; it is not a
      LiveBench field. Records are keyed by LiveBench's own `question_id`, a
      64-character content hash, carried through unchanged, and the file is
      sorted by it.

  Question text and answer text are otherwise unaltered. No question was
  rewritten, translated, truncated or re-answered.


COMPOSITION OF THE SNAPSHOT

  By task:

      math       math_comp        146
      math       olympiad          60
      reasoning  zebra_puzzle     100
      reasoning  spatial           50
                                  ---
                                  356

  By LiveBench release date:

      2024-06-24   176
      2024-07-26    50
      2024-08-31    80
      2024-11-25    50

  180 of the 356 are marked retired: LiveBench has rotated them out of its live
  set, which makes them more likely to have leaked into training corpora. They
  are kept because they roughly double the pool, and because a question's
  measured difficulty is what this project uses it for.


UPSTREAM RIGHTS THAT LIVEBENCH CANNOT GRANT

  LiveBench's Apache-2.0 grant covers LiveBench's own contribution. Three of the
  four subsets rest on someone else's material or someone else's tool, and that
  party's terms travel with the questions. They are carried forward here.

  math_comp (146 questions)
      Derived from the American Mathematics Competitions AMC 12A and 12B 2023
      and the American Invitational Mathematics Examination AIME I and II 2024,
      copyright the Mathematical Association of America; and from the Senior
      Mathematical Challenge 2023, copyright the United Kingdom Mathematics
      Trust. LiveBench rewrote the prose and shuffled the answer order; the
      mathematical content is the original competition content.
      MAA permits copying of its competition problems after the contest for
      non-commercial educational use, provided the MAA copyright notice is
      retained. UKMT permits use of its challenge material within your own
      school or college.

  olympiad (60 questions)
      Derived from the United States of America Mathematical Olympiad 2024
      (copyright the Mathematical Association of America) and the International
      Mathematical Olympiad 2024, including THEIR PUBLISHED SOLUTIONS, with
      formulae masked out and presented as a reordering task.
      This is the highest-exposure subset in the file: it reproduces substantial
      third-party proof text, not merely problem statements. The MAA
      non-commercial educational terms above apply to the USAMO material.

  zebra_puzzle (100 questions)
      Procedurally generated by LiveBench using
      https://github.com/quint-t/Puzzle-Generator-and-Solver. That generator
      carries no licence file and is marked "For non-commercial use only".

  spatial (50 questions)
      Written by the LiveBench authors. No third-party rights are involved, and
      this subset is cleanly covered by the Apache-2.0 grant.


COMMERCIAL USE

  The math_comp and olympiad subsets carry non-commercial terms from their
  upstream owners: the MAA and the UKMT for math_comp, the MAA for the USAMO
  half of olympiad. LiveBench's Apache-2.0 grant does not override those terms,
  because LiveBench never held the rights it would need to grant them away.
  Anyone putting this repository to commercial use should delete those 206
  records from pool.json. The 100 zebra_puzzle records should go with them: the
  generator that produced them is marked non-commercial as well, on weaker
  footing (a line in an unlicensed repository rather than a rights holder's
  published policy) but pointing the same way. That leaves the 50 spatial
  questions, which are the LiveBench authors' own work and carry no such
  restriction. The router's code is MIT and is unaffected either way.


