2. LiteLLM model price table — internal/router/pricedata/prices.json
================================================================================

WHAT IT IS

  internal/router/pricedata/prices.json is a trimmed 387,380-byte snapshot of
  LiteLLM's public model price and context-window table:

      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/main/model_prices_and_context_window.json
      https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm

  It is embedded in the binary and used to seed prices and context windows on a
  manually-entered provider row where the model id matches. Seeding is
  best-effort and never load-bearing: the router measures context itself, and a
  price it cannot find stays zero.

  The file records its own provenance in two top-level fields, `source` and
  `fetched_at`. It covers 2,435 models across 81 providers.

LICENCE

  MIT, which is LiteLLM's own. The full text is at
  internal/router/pricedata/LICENSE-litellm.txt, alongside the snapshot.

  Unlike the LiveBench pool in section 1, there is nothing here that LiteLLM
  does not own. A table of published list prices carries no third-party rights
  to carry forward.

MODIFICATIONS

  Made by this project:

    - Trimmed to five fields per model: the model key, input_cost_per_token,
      output_cost_per_token, max_input_tokens (or max_tokens), and
      litellm_provider. Everything else upstream publishes is dropped.
    - Restricted to rows publishing a per-token price at all, which drops the
      image, audio and embedding rows. Together these take the file from about
      1.75 MB to 378 KB.
    - Re-emitted one model per line with sorted keys, so a refresh produces a
      readable diff rather than a single reflowed blob.

  No price, context window or provider value is altered. Refresh the snapshot
  with `go run . prices fetch`.
